<title>RUSSIA: Russia to change bill, bond series numbers.</title>
<headline>Russia to change bill, bond series numbers.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Central Bank announced on Wednesday changes in the system of numbering new issues of government bonds and treasury bills.</p>
<p>Future T-bill and bond issues will be given series numbers according to the following criteria:</p>
<p>Series number</p>
<p> 21XXX	   -- all short-term discount government obligations</p>
<p>			with a maturity of up to one year, such as</p>
<p>			GKO Treasury bills.</p>
<p> 24XXX	   -- OFZ interest-bearing variable-rate government</p>
<p>			bonds with a maturity from one to five years.</p>
<p> 25XXX	   -- OFZ interest-bearing fixed-rate government</p>
<p>			bonds with a maturity from one to five years.</p>
<p> 26XXX	   -- OFZ interest-bearing fixed-rate government</p>
<p>			bonds with a maturity from five to 30 years.</p>
<p>At present series numbers 21XXX are used only for GKO T-bills with maturities of around three months, 22XXX for T-bills with maturities of around six-12 months, and 23XXX for T-bills with maturities of about 12 months.</p>
<p>Series 24XXX and 25XXX are already in use. No long-term bonds, which would carry the 26XXX series number, have yet been issued.</p>
<p>--Anna Smirnova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
